{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1469024510,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIzMzk2NDEyNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/653#issuecomment-233964126"},"message":"Yaroslav Halchenko wrote:\n\n\u003e just realized that if we start populating with urls pointing to other sources,\n\u003e and some of them would nohow carry information about the executable bit (e.g. a\n\u003e url, unlike a RI pointing to the tarball content, where executable bit is\n\u003e set)... and git doesn't carry an executable bit of the dereferenced content of\n\u003e a symlink, so we e.g. can't add an executable binary under annex, and having a\n\u003e url associated with it hope that somehow annex or git would set an executable\n\u003e bit on it whenever we 'annex get' it. Correct @joeyh?\n\nYes, nothing tracks that.\n\nIn v6 mode, the execute bit of unlocked files is tracked.\n\n## \n\nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1469024825,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIzMzk2NTY2NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/653#issuecomment-233965665"},"message":"On Wed, 20 Jul 2016, Joey Hess wrote:\n\n\u003e    Yaroslav Halchenko wrote:\n\u003e \n\u003e \u003e just realized that if we start populating with urls pointing to other\n\u003e \u003e    sources,\n\u003e \u003e and some of them would nohow carry information about the executable bit\n\u003e \u003e    (e.g. a\n\u003e \u003e url, unlike a RI pointing to the tarball content, where executable bit\n\u003e \u003e    is\n\u003e \u003e set)... and git doesn't carry an executable bit of the dereferenced\n\u003e \u003e    content of\n\u003e \u003e a symlink, so we e.g. can't add an executable binary under annex, and\n\u003e \u003e    having a\n\u003e \u003e url associated with it hope that somehow annex or git would set an\n\u003e \u003e    executable\n\u003e \u003e bit on it whenever we 'annex get' it. Correct @joeyh?\n\u003e \n\u003e    Yes, nothing tracks that.\n\u003e \n\u003e    In v6 mode, the execute bit of unlocked files is tracked.\n\nis it tracked persistently?  i.e. in a clean clone, with content\nfetched from some special remote which doesn't care about executable\nbits, I would get the executable bit set correctly if I unlock the\nfile??\n\nor just while unlocking (set file exec bit as the key's), locking (set\nkey's exec bit as of the file)?\n\n## \n\nYaroslav O. Halchenko\nCenter for Open Neuroscience     http://centerforopenneuroscience.org\nDartmouth College, 419 Moore Hall, Hinman Box 6207, Hanover, NH 03755\nPhone: +1 (603) 646-9834                       Fax: +1 (603) 646-1419\nWWW:   http://www.linkedin.com/in/yarik","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1469028527,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIzMzk4NTU1NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/653#issuecomment-233985554"},"message":"Yaroslav Halchenko wrote:\n\n\u003e is it tracked persistently? i.e. in a clean clone, with content\n\u003e fetched from some special remote which doesn't care about executable\n\u003e bits, I would get the executable bit set correctly if I unlock the\n\u003e file??\n\nIt's persistent, and v6 mode unlocked files get committed as such, so\nare unlocked in all clones.\n\nSee commit b7c8bf5274a64389ac87d6ce0388b8708c261971\n\n## \n\nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1469028634,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIzMzk4NjEzMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/653#issuecomment-233986133"},"message":"On Wed, 20 Jul 2016, Joey Hess wrote:\n\n\u003e    Yaroslav Halchenko wrote:\n\u003e \n\u003e \u003e is it tracked persistently? i.e. in a clean clone, with content\n\u003e \u003e fetched from some special remote which doesn't care about executable\n\u003e \u003e bits, I would get the executable bit set correctly if I unlock the\n\u003e \u003e file??\n\u003e \n\u003e    It's persistent, and v6 mode unlocked files get committed as such, so\n\u003e    are unlocked in all clones.\n\u003e \n\u003e    See commit b7c8bf5274a64389ac87d6ce0388b8708c261971\n\nGreat!  thank you for the explanation/pointer!","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1528797962,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5NjUzNzE5Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/653#issuecomment-396537196"},"message":"As this was FOI, closing after two years.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1528797962,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTY3NTg5MjA3OA=="},"status":2}]}